-- title:
--   Descent of a crossing presentation to a noetherian local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local ring, and let $W$ be a commutative discrete valuation domain which is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal. Fix an irreducible element $\pi \in W$ and an integer $E \ge 1$, and write $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^E)$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\pi^E)$, in which `UVCrossingModel.const (π ^ E) w` denotes the class of the constant series $w$ and `UVCrossingModel.U (π ^ E)`, `UVCrossingModel.V (π ^ E)` are the two distinguished elements whose product is `const (π ^ E) (π ^ E)`. Assume given a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic completion of $R$ onto this model, together with elements $\varpi, g, h \in R$ such that: $\iota$ sends the image of $\varpi$ in the completion to `const (π ^ E) π`; and the ideal $(\varpi, g)$ of $R$, extended to the completion along the canonical map and transported by $\iota$, equals the ideal generated by `const (π ^ E) π` and `U (π ^ E)`, while $(\varpi, h)$ likewise yields the ideal generated by `const (π ^ E) π` and `V (π ^ E)`. Then there are $g', h', w \in R$ with $w$ a unit, $g'h' = \varpi^E w$, $\mathfrak m_R = (\varpi, g', h')$, the ideals $(\varpi, g')$ and $(\varpi, h')$ prime, $h' \notin (\varpi, g')$, $g' \notin (\varpi, h')$, and $(\varpi, g') = (\varpi, g)$, $(\varpi, h') = (\varpi, h)$.
--
--   This descends the standard local model of a node of width $E$ (a singularity of type $A_{E-1}$, as in Deligne–Rapoport and Mazur–Rapoport) from the completion of a noetherian local ring to the ring itself, producing a presentation of the maximal ideal adapted to the two prescribed branch ideals. It is used in the treatment of prolongation tuples at a place of a modular curve, where the two branches through a crossing point and the order of vanishing along them are analysed.
-- source:
